  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `keep_law::narrow_noted` adds a note when the uncut-corner check cannot run.\n- The note text is: `<kind>: the check for corners of the stock tighter than the tool did not run (<error>) - look at the stock corners around the part`.\n- The log line stays. The path is kept. The note does not block the cut.\n- One unit test pins the note.\n- `docs/decisions/2511-corner-check-note.md` records the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe error arm of the corner check wrote only a `tracing::warn!` line.\nThe band check directly above it adds a note in the same case.\nThus material could stay in a corner, and the user saw nothing.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `operation::keep_law::tests::a_corner_check_that_cannot_run_says_so_in_a_note` (`camcraft-app` lib).\n- The test is a unit test because `narrow_noted` is `pub(super)`.\n- The test uses a tool diameter of 4e12 mm. The erosion returns `GeoError::OutOfRange`, and the two checks fail.\n- The test asserts one band note and one corner note. It also asserts that a check that runs adds no \"did not run\" note.\n- Before the fix the pin was red: `the corner check says it did not run: [\"2D Pocket: the check for bands of the stock narrower than the tool did not run (coordinates outside the machinable range) - look at the stock around the part\"]`, `left: 0`, `right: 1`.\n- Mutation: the new `path.notes.push` removed. The pin was red. The line restored. The pin was green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No test gets to the error through the commands or MCP. No legal document makes the corner check fail today.\n- No test makes the corner check fail while the band check passes.\n- The status line and the UI were not run. They show `Toolpath.notes` as they do for the band note.\n- The 0.03 mm noise threshold (`CORNER_HALF_WIDTH`) is not changed. The decision file records the concern of the issue. The review of this number against a measured case stays open work. `Fixes #2511` closes the issue, so that review needs a new issue.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/app/src/operation/keep_law.rs`.\n\nChangelog: A pocket-family operation that clears the stock around the part now says in a note when its uncut-corner check did not run.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2511\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
